 is open:** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp, so borrowing is dearer but still available. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (utility-credit).\n- **Equity is the weak point:** Two utility share offerings were cut back in size. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B equity offering after demand fell short. It is now cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves (pellham-offering).\n- **What this implies:**\n  - Pellham's withdrawal suggests the capex plans rely on a debt-plus-equity mix. Debt alone looks insufficient, or too costly in leverage and credit-rating terms, for the largest spender.\n  - The sources give no data on Pellham's leverage, ratings or bond capacity. I couldn't confirm whether it could close the gap with more debt, so that is a judgment rather than a finding.\n- **Caveats:** The evidence is thin. It covers one bond deal (Norvane), one withdrawn equity deal (Pellham) and a single quarter of spread data. Norvane's smaller capex growth makes it the easier case.","ttft_ms":2922,"type":"result","duration_ms":19206,"uuid":"ac59e891-3e79-4a54-83b7-bd09a6ad85d3","ttft_stream_ms":1526,"time_to_request_ms":76,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":11,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":7,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":7,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":26,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":65,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":205,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":132,"process_rss_mib_result":203,"process_anon_mib_result":122,"process_peak_rss_mib":223,"process_cp